  "evidence": "All published ZIPs have matching registry byte lengths and MD5; all embedded measurement CSV/XLSX files processed using their actual headers and contents. Experiment scenarios in the registry describe the use case. Vehicle commands, motor actuation or a guaranteed sensed close-loop response are not exposed by these network aggregates.",
  "results": [
    "16 ZIPs, each containing a network aggregation file; 3,946 rows total. Five members contain two columns both named senderstationid and their recorded sender values disagree in all 1,196 rows; the destination remains explicit. Only four files provide explicit pairwise interval boundaries (1,000 rows).",
    "The last columns record Transfer and Bandwidth. 3,928/3,946 rows lie within one reported bandwidth unit of 8.192 times the transfer value; this is an internal numeric relationship, not an independent clock reference. Neither a packet sequence nor a receiver delivery time is in those tables. Do not pool rows as physical trips; adjacent files sometimes continue the previous relative interval."
  ],
